07/15/26|07/15/26||CDT|0|F|Y|Chicago|IL|41.8410|-87.6745|OZONE||Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups|Yes|(Discussion Issued 7/15/26 11:45am) The Illinois Environmental Protection Agency has issued a Red Forecast Air Pollution Action Day for Thursday July 16th for the AirNow AQI forecast sectors of Rockford and all 6 Chicago area forecast sectors.  This is in addition to the ongoing Chicago Area Air Pollution Action Day in effect today. This Red Forecast Air Pollution Action Day is declared due to a forecast of Unhealthy-Red category particulates and or ozone on Thursday July 16th.   Northern IL is expected to be on the edge of a thick plume of surface smoke moving in from the north and cleaner air to the south. There is some uncertainty in how far south the smoke progresses and the durations of poor air quality as this dividing line may meander in and out of Northern IL late Wednesday night through Friday.  With this in mind, those with air quality concerns or outdoor plans are encouraged to check current NowCast readings or sign up for EnviroFlash alerts on AirNow.gov.  The AirNow fire and smoke map, https://fire.airnow.gov/, will also show readings from low-cost sensors between regulatory monitoring areas. Further south in the rest of Illinois, surface smoke is less likely but it is possible smoke moves further south than expected for shorter durations of time.  Those outside of Red forecast areas are also encouraged to periodically check current NowCast readings that would indicate surface smoke or sign up for EnviroFlash alerts on AirNow.gov   Note, NowCast AQI readings may show categories higher than the daily forecast to help identify periods of higher 1-hour PM2.5/smoke.  For a description of the differences between daily AQI forecasts and NowCast AQI, visit https://www.airnow.gov/aqi/aqi-basics/using-air-quality-index/ .|Illinois EPA
