h weak high pressure moving in from the north will act to trap pollutants near the surface keeping air quality in that unhealthy range. Ozone should be limited to the moderate range due to the hazy, smoked-filled skies. ***Extended Outlook: USG concentrations of PM2.5 still expected Friday. Skies should start to improve the latter half of Friday with some smoke/hazy skies still occurring the first half of the day due to leftover wildfire smoke with afternoon high temperatures in the low 90s, light northerly winds and mostly sunny skies. Ozone should be limited to the mid to high moderate range depending on how much sunshine filters through the smoke. As a cold front approaches Saturday, there is the potential for scattered showers and storms Saturday afternoon and evening. Temperatures trend slightly downward into the mid to high 80s.Moderate concentrations of ozone and PM2.5 are expected through the weekend with some smoke may be returning next week. Visit airnow.gov or fire.airnow.gov for the most up-to-date AQI information. – VanLenten/Oshinski|Pennsylvania Dept. of Environmental Protection
